<title>CANADA: Bre-X still awaiting Indonesian response.</title>
<headline>Bre-X still awaiting Indonesian response.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bre-X Minerals Ltd and Barrick Gold Corp are still waiting for word from the Indonesian government about their proposal to divide up the huge Busang gold deposit, Bre-X said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're awaiting response from the government,&quot; Bre-X spokesman Steve McAnulty said in a phone interview from Calgary.</p>
<p>Bre-X and Barrick said last week they had submitted a joint proposal to the Indonesian government to split the Busang gold find, but Bre-X said it needed clarification on a few issues.</p>
